1:This is one of those days on which I receive both good news and bad news, one after the other, after midnight.
2:The good news is that although I still haven't figured out what's going on with Ciri, at least I no longer need to worry about oversleeping as I won't need to get up at 6 a.m. in the morning for a while.
3:The bad news is that I couldn't sleep. Whenever I think about the huge task ahead of me when I meet one of the legendary Four Greats today, I just can't seem to fall asleep.
4:In the end, I spent half the night on CatChat and ended up reading about the Asaha High School pool party extensively, finding out 80% of what happened there. When I accidentally liked one of the selfies while swiping the screen, I learned the remaining 20% from Nana Shiraishi, who was also staying up late.
5:Human beings have many chances to share their joys and sorrows with each other. I can only say that I've worn myself out for Soul and Strix...
6:But I can't help it since I'm a kind and upright person who would do anything for my friends.
7:Time always passes quickly at night. When the first ray of dawn shines into my room through cracks in the loosely drawn curtains, I finally feel ready to fall asleep.
8:My phone slips out of my hand while I'm drifting off, and its solid screen smacks me hard in the face. After that, it starts vibrating as if some strange switch has been turned on.
9:I pick it up quickly and look at the screen. Fortunately, there are only two text messages.
10:Noah
11:{character:Noah}(Text message) Don't forget that you're having afternoon tea with Kurone Toujou today.
12:{character:Noah}(Text message) I'll come over in 26 minutes to pick you up for styling.
13:player
14:{character:player}(Text Message) Styling?
15:Is she saying what I think she's saying? Noah's words wake me up instantly like a bucket of cold water has been poured over my head.
16:{character:Noah}(Text message) I'll take you to pick a set of suitable clothes, then you'll need some decent makeup.
17:{character:player}(Text Message) Wouldn't that be too over the top? After all, this is afternoon tea we're talking about here--the type that ends in two to three hours.
18:{character:Noah}(Text message) You've already spent a fortune buying those cut flowers. You'll look really suspicious if you're not dressed appropriately.
19:{character:Noah}(Text message) Strix owns a clothing business. We can go there to get you a whole set of clothes.
20:{character:player}(Text Message) Your words are making me nervous. I feel like I'm attending a business gala now.
21:{character:Noah}(Text message) Just so you know, I'll be at your place in 21 minutes. You should have enough time to wash up if you get out of bed now.
22:{character:player}(Text Message) I'm not awake yet!
23:{character:Noah}(Text message) 20 minutes.
24:My experience tells me that the wise thing to do is to get up now...
25:Noah's time management skills are simply insane. She'll definitely arrive on time. Among all the people I know, the only other person who is capable of doing this is that emotionless work machine Osamu Saitou.
26:The moment we meet, Noah drags me outside efficiently and stuffs me into the familiar-looking red car that disappeared quickly from my sight like a bolt of lightning yesterday.
27:The car drives to a low-key but luxurious clothing store. When I look up at the entrance, I can see the name of the store, Chaque Jour, spelled out in huge, sleek gold letters on a black background on its door, which is decorated with hollow carvings.
28:It turns out that this clothing store, which has appeared in major fashion magazines recently, is actually owned by Strix?! Suddenly, I find it extremely difficult to associate the information dealer with fashion.
29:Probably because my doubts are in plain sight on my face, Noah actively starts explaining.
30:{character:Noah}(Text message) Do you feel that this place doesn't match the image of the boss and Strix?
31:{character:Noah}(Text message) Actually, you can trust the taste of information dealers. The selection in this store and their designs are the result of the hard work of some Strix members who visited more than 20 countries over 15 months and compared tens of thousands of sets of data.
32:{character:Noah}(Text message) The clothes sold in Chaque Jour will lead fashion trends for the next five years at least.
33:The data is very convincing, and I suddenly feel like I understand.
34:We are greeted by two young female shop assistants after we enter the store. Without asking too many questions, they take us to the dressing room in a corner on the second floor where three sets of outfits are neatly hung.
35:{character:Noah}(Text message) They have been told the situation before we arrived. They prepared these clothes for you, so pick one of them.
36:I look at the three sets of clothing with completely different styles in front of me. It's time to make another decision that will decide my destiny...
37:I consider the environment of Countless Springs. I remember that it is a classical and elegant place, so I decide to choose a formal suit with simple and elegant colors.
38:The moment I exit the dressing room in the clothes, Noah comes up to me and scrutinizes my appearance from all angles, frowning from time to time. She seems to be in a dilemma over something.
39:It isn't long before she lowers her head, taps her mobile phone a few times, and shows the assistant next to her. I think Noah must have made a request. When the assistant returns, I see that she is carrying a few dark green ribbons and a toolbox. She then hands the items to Noah.
40:Noah pats me on the back and motions me to stand still. Out of the corner of my eye, I see her take some materials out of the toolbox and start to fiddle with the corner of my clothes. However, I couldn't see what she did because my view was blocked.
41:It wasn't until she pulled on my shirt to smooth out the folds on it that I realized there is now a strip of dark green patterned fabric around the hem of the simple clothes. The abstract and free style of the lotus leaf patterns of the fabric complements this outfit well.
42:{character:player}What superb craftsmanship! You're as amazing as I expected!
43:I can't tell if my praise makes Noah happy or not, but I suddenly receive a text message after we say goodbye to the assistant and get inside the car.
44:{character:Noah}(Text message) My mother is a painter. This is nothing to me, so you don't need to be so surprised.
45:I'm a little curious. Judging from the changes she made to the clothes, Noah should have inherited her mother's artistic genes, so how did she end up becoming an information dealer instead of pursuing a career in art?
46:But I see that she has already started playing a game and has no intention to talk, so I give up on asking her about this.
47:After we arrive at Countless Springs, a staff member politely guides us to the VIP guest rooms.
50:Noah pats my shoulder after the staff member leaves.
50:{character:Staff}Noah pats my shoulder after the staff member leaves.
51:{character:Noah}(Text message) You go by yourself. I'll wait for you outside.
52:{character:player}Is that okay? Should we discuss this with the staff again?
53:{character:Noah}(Text message)No. I can grind this in-game event while I'm here. A turn-based game is launching its open beta today. I want to be ranked at the top of the rankings.
54:I want to complain that she can achieve that by simply spending money in the game. But then I thought of a possible reason for her. There are usually various options such as a basic battle pass, a premium battle pass, server launch packs, and double rewards for the first top-up... It might be necessary to be in an environment where no one will interrupt you to calculate the most effective spending plan before buying everything.
55:It looks like I'll be responsible for communicating with others.
56:The staff returns soon, and I follow him out of the VIP room into the winding corridors. I can't help but notice that the internal structure of Countless Springs is really complicated. The tortuous corridor here is already an effective security barrier.
57:After walking for about ten minutes, we arrive at a simple and elegant door.
59:After the staff leaves, I open the door and enter an extremely elegantly decorated room. Someone seems to be sitting in the middle of the room behind a screen painted with birds singing in a bamboo forest. The light shining in from the window casts the person's shadow on the screen. The figure looks like it belongs to a woman. This person should be Kurone Toujou.
60:Kurone Toujou
61:{character:Kurone Toujou}Good afternoon. It's so nice to meet you. I'm Kurone Toujou, the manager of Countless Springs.
62:{character:Kurone Toujou}Refreshments and seating arrangements have been made for you. It would be my honor if they are satisfactory to you.
63:The voice coming from behind the screen speaks softly and pleasantly in the local dialect, sounding like the singing of an oriole. One can only imagine how incredible she would sound when she is singing. However, the estranged tone in her voice makes me feel like she is a snow lotus in the distant mountains.
64:{character:player}Hi, I'm {var:player_nickname}.
65:On a low coffee table facing the screen are several plates of exquisite and delicious snacks and some tea, which must be the refreshments and seating arrangements she mentioned. I walk up and sit down on the soft cushion beside the low coffee table, and think about what I should say to her.
66:As if she can sense how reserved I'm feeling, Kurone Toujou chuckles from behind the screen and starts making conversation with me instead, which eases the tension in the air.
67:{character:Kurone Toujou}I've heard that the other members of the Four Greats have entertained an esteemed guest who is good at playing mahjong recently. I believe that must be you.
68:{character:player}I wouldn't say I'm an esteemed guest, but I did play some mahjong with Lily Kitahara and Kazuha Saionji.
69:{character:Kurone Toujou}You're too modest. If possible, I hope you can come to the East Wind dojo I operate to play some mahjong when you are free.
70:{character:Kurone Toujou}We all have a different playing style, so the dojos we operate are all good at different styles of play. Perhaps you'll find a mahjong style that suits you better after trying more new things.
71:{character:player}I see, so what's your playing style like, Miss Toujou?
72:{character:Kurone Toujou}Hehe, you're such an interesting person. We'll meet at a mahjong table eventually, so it'll be dangerous for me to reveal my playing style in advance. After all, psychological warfare is very important in a mahjong match.
73:{character:Kurone Toujou}But if we do get the chance to play a game together, I'm looking forward to you learning another side of me, Kurone Toujou, through mahjong.
74:Kurone Toujou's friendly manner makes me relax. Now that I'm no longer so nervous, I have the energy to observe everything around me, such as the teacup in my hand.
75:The bottom feels uneven, as if something is written on there. Driven by my curiosity, after drinking the tea inside the teacup, I turn it upside down to take a quick glance at the bottom and see a familiar logo with the character "Yu".
76:I think about where I've seen it before. Suddenly, I remember seeing the exact same logo on a painting of eight beauties on the wall of the mahjong room when I visited Strix for the first time.
77:{character:Kurone Toujou}Do you not like the refreshments?
78:{character:player}Ah, no, it's not that. I just suddenly have a question.
79:{character:Kurone Toujou}I'm all ears if you're willing to tell me about it.
80:Kurone Toujou's words interrupt my thoughts, reminding me of the heavy burden I bear and that I'm not here to eat, drink, and be merry. I think I'll start by asking about the tournament of the Mahjong Soul Shrine because I've become really interested in this legendary competition after so many people have told me stories about it.
81:{character:player}Miss Toujou, if it's okay with you, can you tell me when the next Mahjong Soul Shrine tournament will start?
82:Instead of answering my question directly, Kurone Toujou ponders it for a while before asking me a question in return.
83:{character:Kurone Toujou}In your eyes, what kind of existence is the priestess of the Mahjong Soul Shrine?
84:The priestess of the Mahjong Soul Shrine? She must be referring to Ichihime. I think about what she's like in everyday life...
85:...She doesn't have a worry in the world, and her stomach seems to be connected to a black hole.
86:But that's not all. She seems able to keep the Mahjong Soul Shrine in order while being on guard against Wanjirou's slacking-off behavior and preventing Kaguyahime from causing mischief.
87:{character:player}Ichihime is very competent as a priestess of the Mahjong Soul Shrine, it's just that... she has a really good appetite.
88:Despite the fact that she often causes situations that are both frustrating and amusing, it is precisely because of her warm and courageous character.
89:Why does she have a dog-like personality even though she's clearly a cat-like creature? Anyway, that doesn't matter.
90:{character:player}Ichihime is a kind and warm priestess. Everyone likes her a lot.
91:After I finish speaking, I hear a clear and melodious laughter coming from behind the screen. She seems to be in a good mood.
92:{character:Kurone Toujou}It seems that the rumor about you having a good relationship with the priestess is true.
93:{character:Kurone Toujou}Although it's true that she really does act like that now, I vaguely remember that she was... more indifferent when she participated in the tournament back then.
94:{character:player}Huh? An indifferent Ichihime... I'm actually a little curious about what that's like.
95:{character:Kurone Toujou}Hehe, I believe you'll find out eventually, given your relationship with her.
96:{character:Kurone Toujou}When you see the other side of the priestess, you'll naturally know that the mahjong tournament will be starting soon.
97:I find it so difficult to imagine what this other side of Ichihime is like. Is it possible that Ichihime will become serious and solemn when the tournament starts?
98:I imagine Ichihime wearing a pair of glasses and holding a teacher's pointer, shuttling through mahjong tables as she strictly instructs everyone to play mahjong, but this image doesn't seem real to me.
99:{character:Kurone Toujou}Don't take my word for it though. You should just treat this as a story.
100:{character:player}What do you mean?
101:{character:Kurone Toujou}It seems that I and everyone else who participated in the tournament have a vague memory of what happened back then. This is just a feeling I've always had.
102:{character:Kurone Toujou}Ten years have passed in the blink of an eye. Sometimes, even I wonder whether this is reality or just my imagination.
103:Kurone Toujou falls silent after speaking, as if she is lost in her memories. After a long time, she speaks leisurely again and asks me a question.
104:{character:Kurone Toujou}What would you think if a person's temperament suddenly changes and seems to become a different person?
105:After thinking about it, I feel like this kind of thing is quite common. For example, it's only when a friend who is usually cheerful and talkative has a breakdown that you realize they have always been under tremendous pressure, or when you only realize after a kind colleague leaves their job that your relationship has only been good because they have always been accommodating you one-sidedly...
106:{character:player}I remember a saying about how a person only needs an instant to break down. Everyone wears too many masks for work, studies, and various activities in daily life.
107:{character:player}That's why we often don't expose others even if we know they are wearing a mask. It's because everyone has their own difficulties.
108:{character:player}What's more, if someone is willing to show you their true self, doesn't that mean we are people who trust each other the most?
109:{character:Kurone Toujou}You're more open-minded than I imagined. No wonder I feel so relaxed and happy when I'm with you. It must be the influence of your emotional state.
110:Recently, there have been similar stories in the news on social media, such as stories about how neighbors who are usually kind are secretly killing small animals, or how a colleague who seems to be close to you is secretly snitching about you to your boss every day... Ah, I have to stop thinking about this. It's very easy for such negative news to make people panic.
111:{character:player}I think... it's easier to get along with people who are the same on the inside and the outside.
112:{character:Kurone Toujou}Indeed... People who are the same on the inside and the outside give others a sense of security, which makes it easier to get along with each other.
113:During the remaining time, Kurone Toujou and I chat a lot about mahjong, and I learned a lot from her insights on mahjong.
114:Before I know it, it's already time for the afternoon tea to end, and a staff member is already at the door.
115:Kurone Toujou is both skilled at reading people's moods and finding things to talk about. I get the feeling that any person can have a very pleasant time here with her. I think this is what makes her so charming and why everyone wants to have afternoon tea with her.
116:I get up and prepare to leave. When I say goodbye to Kurone Toujou, she suddenly asks me about my clothes.
117:{character:Kurone Toujou}The pattern at the hem of the clothes you're wearing today is unique and ingenious. Can you tell me which famous designer did this?
118:I think about the sensitive nature of Noah's identity as a core member of Strix, so I tell her the address of Chaque Jour.
119:{character:Kurone Toujou}Thank you for sharing this information with me. I simply must go shopping at a shop that can make such good designs.
120:When I finally leave Countless Springs, Noah is already waiting for me at the entrance.
121:After returning to Chaque Jour with her by car and changing into my own clothes, I get ready to tell her everything I saw and heard today. Suddenly, she carefully removes something from the shoulder of the clothes I just changed out of.
122:{character:Noah}(Text message) This is a spy camera. It has recorded everything that happened today, so you don't need to report anything back to me.
123:Just as I'm about to ask her when she planted the camera on me, I suddenly remembered that she patted this exact spot on my shoulder just before I went to see Kurone Toujou.
124:I feel like saying something, but then I stop myself. After swallowing the things I want to say to her, I decide to give up. I should have already gotten used to the way Strix does things over these last few days anyway.
125:The good side of this is that I won't need to report on this to Kutsuji in person.
126:This set of bright-colored clothes is very eye-catching in terms of both color and style among the three sets, so it naturally catches my attention too.
127:The moment I exit the dressing room in the clothes, Noah comes up to me and scrutinizes my appearance from all angles, frowning from time to time. She seems to be in a dilemma over something.
128:It isn't long before she lowers her head, taps her mobile phone a few times, and shows the assistant next to her. I think Noah must have made a request. When the assistant returns, I see that she is carrying several pieces of translucent tulle and a toolbox. She then hands the items to Noah.
129:Only after she straightens the folds by pulling my lapels do I realize that she has cut and folded the tulle into butterflies of various sizes and placed them at various seams of the jacket to neutralize the exuberance from the collision of colors and add a bit of elegance.
130:{character:Noah}(Text message) Countless Springs is a place where it's really easy to get into trouble. It's not a good thing to dress too ostentatiously.
131:{character:Noah}(Text message) What's more, it's better to dress a little more solemnly to meet Kurone Toujou, so I just made slight adjustments.
132:Staff
133:{character:Staff}Please wait here while we complete the preparations.
134:{character:Staff}Also, as this afternoon tea is only for one guest, you two can discuss who will be going.
135:The staff returns soon. I follow him out of the VIP room, and we arrive at a garden after we pass through the hall where the auction was held yesterday.
136:I must admit that Countless Springs is really massive. As I look at the large artificial lake in the rear garden, I gradually understand why the tickets are so expensive.
137:The staff takes me to a pavilion in the middle of the artificial lake. Someone seems to be sitting in the center behind a screen painted with birds singing in a bamboo forest. From the silhouette, it is vaguely discernible that this person is a woman. That should be Kurone Toujou.
138:The staff leaves without saying a word after signaling that I have arrived. In this situation, I suddenly don't know what to say.
139:As if the person behind the screen can sense my distress, she laughs and comforts me.
140:{character:Kurone Toujou}When I heard that your clothes are as beautiful as flowers today, I suddenly felt like I wanted to admire the beauty of flowers, so I arbitrarily decided to have afternoon tea here in this pavilion instead. I hope you don't mind.
141:Her voice is soft and pleasant, like the singing of an oriole, and it feels difficult to say no to any request she may make. However, the estranged tone in her voice makes me feel like she is a snow lotus in the distant mountains.
142:{character:player}That's alright. The scenery is really beautiful here. I love it.
143:{character:Kurone Toujou}I feel so relieved. Here are your refreshments and seat. I hope these are also to your liking.
144:On a stone table facing the screen are several plates of exquisite and delicious snacks and some tea, which must be the refreshments and seating arrangements she mentioned. I walk up and sit down on a chair beside the stone table and think about what we should chat about later.
145:{character:Kurone Toujou}Although you already know who I am, to be polite, I should introduce myself to you again. I am Kurone Toujou, the person who runs Countless Springs. It is my honor to have afternoon tea with you today.
146:{character:player}I'm {var:player_nickname}, and it's also my honor to have afternoon tea with you today, Miss Toujou.
147:{character:Kurone Toujou}Hehe, chatting with you is such a pleasant experience. I think we'll have an enjoyable afternoon today.
148:{character:Kurone Toujou}This is the garden behind Countless Springs. I believe this is your first time here.
149:{character:player}Yeah.
150:{character:Kurone Toujou}The lotus flowers planted in the lake are all varieties that we bred ourselves here at Countless Springs. There are about 20 varieties, but some have already bloomed and withered due to their different flowering periods.
151:I look towards the lake in response to her words and see many green lotus pods, some of which are blooming very beautifully. A breeze blows over from the lake, carrying bursts of a calming elegant floral fragrance with it.
152:When I look at the rock garden in the middle of the lake, I see a very familiar logo with the character "Yu". It caught my attention because I saw the exact same logo on a painting of eight beauties on the wall of the mahjong room when I visited Strix for the first time.
153:{character:Kurone Toujou}What are you thinking? Can you share your thoughts with me?
154:Kurone Toujou's words interrupt my thoughts, reminding me of the heavy burden I bear and that I'm not here to eat, drink, and be merry. However, I do remember one thing when she asked me this question.
155:When I was chatting with Saturne earlier, he asked me a question: "If there is usually only one winner in a mahjong game, why were the Four Greats evenly matched in the last tournament?" I think it's best to ask one of the persons concerned for the answer to this question.
156:After considering my words carefully, I consult Kurone Toujou about the matter. She falls silent for a moment before answering.
157:{character:Kurone Toujou}Actually, my memories of everything related to the tournament are very vague... I only have some rough impressions.
158:{character:Kurone Toujou}But I can actually answer your question. According to the rules of the tournament, we played four Hanchan matches, and we each won first place once.
159:{character:Kurone Toujou}And when we finally settled the points for the last game, we all got zero points, so there was no winner in that game.
160:{character:Kurone Toujou}As the organizer trusted our skill, they named us the Four Greats even though there was no champion in that tournament. At the same time, we each gained the right to inherit one of the four dojos: East Wind, South Wind, West Wind, and North Wind.
161:She starts smiling suddenly and then complains jokingly to me with her soft voice.
162:{character:Kurone Toujou}When I inherited the East Wind dojo, I thought it was a big dojo. I didn't expect it to be a dojo that had fallen into disuse for a long time.
163:{character:Kurone Toujou}It took me a lot of effort to make the East Wind dojo flourish like it is now with its own students.
164:The dojo has its own students. That detail caught my attention. The dojos I usually go to only let people play mahjong there. I've been invited to go to the North Wind and West Wind dojos managed by Lily Kitahara and Kazuha Saionji several times before, but even then we only played mahjong together at the same table. I never noticed that they could accept students.
165:{character:player}What do you mean when you say it has its own students? Do you mean that you can teach others to play mahjong there?
166:{character:Kurone Toujou}Yes. Of all the dojos in One Han City, only the Four Winds dojos, namely the East Wind, South Wind, West Wind, and North Wind dojos are qualified to teach others to play mahjong.
167:{character:Kurone Toujou}Each of these dojo is divided into two parts. You must be so focused on playing mahjong every time that you haven't noticed this. After ordinary guests enter the hall from the main entrance, a receptionist will guide them to a mahjong table to play games.
168:{character:Kurone Toujou}The dojo's own students enter through the side door with an access card and go directly to the place where they will be taught. Each dojo teaches students in a different place. For example, the East Wind dojo is designed as a traditional wooden building with only three floors.
169:{character:Kurone Toujou}There is only an ordinary dojo on the first floor. The students are taught on the second floor, and even I go there to review game logs for everyone occasionally.
170:{character:Kurone Toujou}As for the third floor, let me keep that a secret from you for now. I'll introduce it to you when you visit the East Wind dojo one day.
171:{character:player}In that case, I'll definitely come to have a look when I get the chance.
172:{character:player}Is the same thing taught at each of the Four Winds dojos?
173:{character:Kurone Toujou}They pretty much teach the same skills. What makes them different is their concept of mahjong.
174:{character:Kurone Toujou}The East Wind dojo advocates that one should enjoy the process of playing mahjong without caring too much about the result. Um... Our students say that we have more of a "Zen-like" approach to playing mahjong.
175:{character:Kurone Toujou}The South Wind dojo advocates that mahjong competitions are a commercial means and believes that there's nothing you can't resolve by playing mahjong.
176:{character:Kurone Toujou}The West Wind dojo advocates that competition is a means to continuously improve and hone one's mahjong skills. This dojo often invites the other three dojos to have competitions. In fact, we just had a mahjong contest a few days ago.
177:{character:Kurone Toujou}The North Wind dojo advocates that mahjong is the embodiment of desire and that the purpose of competition is to win.
178:{character:Kurone Toujou}As each dojo has a different concept of mahjong, the students that gather in these four dojos are also different. The only thing that is the same for all of them is that they all work hard for their own ideals.
179:{character:Kurone Toujou}If you want, you can join one of our dojos based on your mahjong-related beliefs. I think you would be a powerful addition to whichever dojo you join.
180:When Kurone Toujou talks about the Four Winds dojos, I suddenly remember the legend of the seven wonder dojos of One Han City that Fu Ji told me about. Maybe they are related in some way.
181:{character:player}Fu Ji told me that One Han City has seven wonder dojos. Is that true?
182:{character:Kurone Toujou}There are indeed seven legendary dojos in One Han City. Although I don't really understand how they became known as the seven wonder dojos over time, hehe.
183:{character:Kurone Toujou}The seven dojos correspond to the Four Winds and Three Dragons tiles, which are East, South, West, North, White, Green, and Red.
184:{character:player}Is it possible that Four Winds corresponds to the Four Winds dojos, namely the East Wind, South Wind, West Wind, and North Wind dojos?
185:{character:Kurone Toujou}Hehe, yes.
186:{character:player}Which three dojos do the Three Dragons correspond to?
187:{character:Kurone Toujou}Why don't you say the name of Fu Ji's dojo out loud?
188:{character:player}Luck and Fortune?
189:{character:Kurone Toujou}Hehe, wouldn't you agree that Luck and Fortune represent the tile Green which has the character for prosperity on it? In terms of being a wonder, Fu Ji herself might be one of the reasons why it is one of the wonder dojos.
190:{character:Kurone Toujou}It's possible that Fu Ji was already the master of Luck and Fortune before I became the master of East Wind dojo. No one knows how she inherited that dojo. She might even be the founder.
191:I think of the rumor concerning Fu Ji's age and decide that it might actually be possible. But since I can't verify her age, I can only guess.
192:{character:player}What about the other two?
193:{character:Kurone Toujou}The one representing Red is located near the Mahjong Soul Shrine. It is a fixed venue where the Mahjong Soul Shrine holds tournaments and is usually only open to the public during that time. The time when the tournament starts, however, depends on the mood of the priest.
 194:{character:player}It looks like our priest is very casual.
195:{character:Kurone Toujou}Hehe, yes.
196:{character:Kurone Toujou}As for the last dojo that represents White, even I'm not sure where it is. All I've heard is that it has been abandoned for many years.
197:{character:player}Why was it abandoned?
198:{character:Kurone Toujou}No one knows the exact reason. In fact, all everyone knows is that it exists. It is a legendary dojo in the truest sense.
199:{character:player}Has no one tried to find it during all these years?
200:{character:Kurone Toujou}I don't know about that. Perhaps some people do chase after legendary things, but whether they can find something so mystical with no evidence of its existence is another matter.
201:{character:Kurone Toujou}The tulle design at the seams of the clothes you're wearing today is very novel... It looks like a custom order instead of a common branded item bought on the market.
202:{character:Kurone Toujou}Can you tell me which famous designer did this?
203:{character:player}You can even tell that?
204:{character:Kurone Toujou}Hehe, how embarrassing. Many esteemed guests come to Countless Springs every day, so my familiarity with all kinds of luxury brands is essentially one of my basic abilities now. However, the brand design you're wearing isn't something I'm familiar with.
205:{character:player}It's from a store called Chaque Jour. It's quite popular in One Han City recently.
206:Clothes should be comfortable to wear, and the style of this outfit is also very trendy. The common craftsmanship of adding a pattern to a sweater hasn't been used. Judging from the fine and traditional stitches, they seem to have been stitched together by hand instead of by machine, which has crude stitchwork and makes mistakes.
208:{character:player}This design is quite thoughtful.
209:Noah gives me a disapproving look. After frowning at me cutely, she sends a text message to me to ask me about something.
210:{character:Noah}(Text message) Are you sure you want to wear this? Aren't you hot?
211:After listening to Noah, I think about it carefully...
212:I touch the fabric. It's soft and extremely breathable, and it goes together very well with the T-shirt worn inside.
213:{character:player}I've decided. I'll get this one. It'll be easy to move around in.
214:{character:Noah}(Text message) Choose whatever you want. You're lucky it isn't that hot today.
215:After taking some time to change, we drive to Countless Springs.
216:The staff returns soon. I follow him out of the VIP room. We pass by an artificial lake filled with lotus flowers after we go through the hall where the auction was held yesterday. In the end, we arrive at the entrance of a three-story building by the lake, and a staff member takes me to the top floor.
217:{character:Staff}Miss Toujou is waiting for you inside. I'll be off now. May you have a pleasant afternoon.
218:I observe the situation from the entrance after he leaves. The entrance is an arch without doors, so I can see directly inside.
219:Not far from the window is a screen painted with birds singing in a bamboo forest. The figure moving behind it appears to belong to a woman. This person should be Kurone Toujou.
220:While I think about what to say, a voice travels over from behind the screen.
221:{character:Kurone Toujou}This is the highest place in Countless Springs, and it offers a panoramic view of the lake and water.
222:{character:Kurone Toujou}At the same time, it's also very cool here because of the terrain. It's a nice place to cool down in this season. I hope you don't mind that I arranged to have our afternoon tea here instead.
223:Kurone Toujou's voice is soft and pleasant, like the singing of an oriole, and it feels difficult to say no to any request she may make. However, the estranged tone in her voice makes me feel like she is a snow lotus in the distant mountains.
224:On a round wooden table facing the screen are several plates of exquisite and delicious snacks and some tea, which must be the refreshments and seating arrangements she mentioned. I walk up and sit down on a chair beside the stone table and think about what we should chat about later.
225:To my surprise, I hear a soft cry from behind the screen just before a white fluffy ball rushes to the table in front of me and sticks out a pink tongue to lick the tea in my teacup.
226:When it looks up at me, I realize that it's a snow-white fox that looks very young. I look at the weather outside and the creature in front of me, and feel a little surprised.
227:This should be the season in which silver foxes molt, so I can't believe it looks so... snowy white and cute. If it isn't a miracle, then they must have some special way of taking care of it. Of course, it's possible that some animals don't need to molt here in One Han City.
228:Kurone Toujou apologizes to me while calling the name of the little fox softly and waiting for it to return behind the screen. That's how I learned that this little fox is called "Snowy Dumpling," which is very appropriate for it.
229:But Snowy Dumpling has a mind of its own. It picks up a pastry from in front of me and runs away along the window sill on the third floor.
230:{character:Kurone Toujou}Um... I'm sorry, can you let me deal with something first?
231:{character:player}What's wrong?
232:{character:Kurone Toujou}It hasn't been long since Snowy Dumpling has been weaned off milk. I shouldn't have brought it with me, but it doesn't want to leave my side today, so there's nothing I can do about it...
233:{character:Kurone Toujou}It's run off by itself, and it might be in danger if I don't find it in time. After all, there are many guests here at Countless Springs, and there are also several guard dogs in the courtyard.
234:Kurone Toujou speaks anxiously and keeps apologizing for the bad experience after speaking. In this sudden situation...
235:I look at the clothes I'm wearing. Sure enough, I had a lot of foresight when I chose this set. Snowy Dumpling can't have gone that far away since it has such short arms and legs. Instead of sitting here and worrying, it would be better to go downstairs to help Kurone Toujou look for it.
236:{character:player}I'll go. It shouldn't have gotten that far away.
237:{character:Kurone Toujou}But... you're a guest I invited here. It would be too rude to make you help me with this. I'll ask staff members to search for it.
238:{character:player}It's alright. You can get staff members to help search for it together. I'll see if Snowy Dumpling is still nearby.
239:{character:Kurone Toujou}Well... I really am worried about it. In that case, I'll be brazen enough to ask you for help this time.
240:I encounter several staff members downstairs. Kurone Toujou must have called them here to help find the little fox together.
241:{character:Staff}You're not familiar with the terrain here, so you can help us search around here. Let us search the more distant places.
242:{character:player}Okay.
243:I walk around the small building into well-tended gardens with many berry trees. It is quite difficult to find a little fox in this environment as it will not be easy to spot if it hides among the flowers.
244:Luckily, the pastry it took before it left is quite crumbly, so I manage to follow an intermittent trail of crumbs all the way to a small clearing in the center of the garden.
245:After I approach it, I see that Snowy Dumpling really is here. Most of the pastry has been eaten, and there are crumbs all over the floor. Meanwhile, Snowy Dumpling is now playing by chasing its tail in the clearing.
246:It seems a little frightened when it sees me, but it doesn't hide from me. Instead, it looks at me cautiously like a child who has done something wrong.
247:I step over a bush in front of me and try to pick it up when I hear someone talking nearby as they pass by. It looks like a man and a woman, but I can't hear what they are saying because they are quite far away.
248:Just as I look up, the woman who I heard talking just happened to come to the corner and face my direction. This woman is Ciri, the reason why I came here.
249:The man next to her is wearing hats, masks, and sunglasses, which makes it impossible for me to see his face clearly. Judging from Ciri's expression, they are obviously arguing about something, and their conversation isn't going well.
250:Before long, Ciri leaves quickly first. After she leaves, the man glances in my direction and leaves after her.
251:I make a mental note of his clothing even though it has no recognizable features. With Snow Dumpling in my arms, I return to the third floor to where Kurone Toujou is.
252:Seeing us come up, Kurone Toujou thanks me politely, then she lowers her voice and tells Snowy Dumpling to get behind the screen. I start worrying about it because her tone is a little cold, so I focus on my ears and listen to their voices from over there.
253:To my surprise, instead of scolding Snowy Dumpling coldly like someone self-important, her voice is filled with warmth and concern and sounds quite gentle.
254:Seeing Kurone Toujou act so amiably and gently changes my initial impression of her.
255:My only regret is that the snacks and tea on my table have been replaced with something else. Although all the snacks served at Countless Springs are delicious, what you don't have always seems nicer. The new snacks don't look as delicious as the one that Snowy Dumpling took away. I only have myself to blame for being too slow.
256:Hesitate, and you'll lose. Hold yourself back, and you'll miss out on things.
257:The afternoon tea session ends soon. Before I leave, a staff member comes over and hands me an exquisite box of snacks.
258:{character:Kurone Toujou}Among the snacks we prepared for your afternoon tea is a pastry called "hundred flower crisp" which is extremely complicated to make. This pastry is a specialty of Countless Springs that is usually only prepared for esteemed guests.
259:{character:Kurone Toujou}I didn't expect this little baby to destroy it. There wasn't enough time to make another one, so we could only give you normal snacks to eat.
260:{character:player}Actually, those snacks were very delicious too. I like them.
261:{character:Kurone Toujou}Hehe, that's great to hear. But I still wanted you to have a taste of this famous pasty of Countless Springs, so I asked the kitchen to make you another batch while we were chatting. If you don't mind, you can take it home and taste it later.
262:{character:Kurone Toujou}I... wanted to give you some beautiful memories today, but my hospitality was terrible in the end.
263:{character:player}My memories of today are beautiful. Snow Dumpling is very cute, and I also got to see a different side of you that I had never imagined, Miss Toujou.
264:{character:Kurone Toujou}A different side of me, huh... Hehe, in that case, please play mahjong with me at the East Wind dojo when you get the chance. I'll also be happy for the opportunity to get closer to you.
265:{character:player}I'll definitely come if I get the chance.
266:When I leave Countless Springs, I see Noah already waiting for me at the entrance.
267:After I change out of the clothes at Chaque Jour, she bustles around me like a hardworking bee.
268:First she makes me sit on the sofa, then she puts a mobile phone stand on the table in front of me and arranges a mobile phone so that it faces me, and then she adjusts the angle again.
269:After everything is ready, she gives me a big thumbs up. Immediately, I see an arrogant face appear on the screen of the mobile phone.
270:Kutsuji
271:{character:Kutsuji}According to the original plan, you would be able to go home already, but because you lost the spy camera that you were wearing, you'll have to tell me everything that happened today.
272:{character:player}When did you put a camera on me?
273:He glances at Noah beside me, after which, she pats my shoulder. Suddenly, I remember that she also patted me there before I went to meet Kurone Toujou. So that's when it happened.
274:After sighing, I tell him everything that happened today after I separated from Noah, including the part about seeing Ciri in the garden.
275:Surprisingly, Kutsuji, who usually has a lot to say, actually listens carefully to me, frowning from time to time as if he is thinking about something. It takes me half an hour to finish the story, and I find myself feeling strange that he didn't interrupt me at all during this time.
276:I'm not familiar with the terrain of Countless Springs, so I might cause them more trouble if I get lost while searching for the fox.
277:While I'm hesitating, a staff member rushes over and replaces the snacks and tea in front of me that Snow Dumpling ruined. After that, Kurone Toujou instructs the staff to leave.
278:{character:Kurone Toujou}I'm really sorry about this accident. I've already asked them to search for Snow Dumpling.
279:{character:Kurone Toujou}You should just relax and enjoy the snacks. But... *Sigh* Among the snacks we prepared for your afternoon tea is a pastry called "hundred flower crisp" that is extremely complicated to make. This pastry is a specialty of Countless Springs that is usually only prepared for esteemed guests.
280:{character:Kurone Toujou}I specially wanted you to try it, but that little baby destroyed it.
281:Although I feel like it's a shame, I just can't criticize a woman who is apologizing sincerely. I can only say that there's an element of luck in this matter, just like when playing mahjong.
282:I get up and prepare to leave Countless Springs after the staff reminds me to leave. Noah is already waiting for me at the entrance.
283:After I return home, I decline a bunch of mahjong invitations and collapse on my bed, probably because I'm so tired and relieved after completing the task.
284:Suddenly, I receive a text message from Kutsuji.
285:{character:Kutsuji}(Text message) I'm very pleased with your performance today. I'll come and pick you up to complete the last part of the transaction in a few days.
286:To be honest, I actually don't know what useful information he got from this process. The closer I get to these legendary Four Greats, the more mysteries there seem to be. Moreover, these mysteries collide and merge with each other to create new mysteries.
287:Perhaps I'll find out the truth of all these things one day. I gradually fall asleep with this thought in mind.
